{
  "name": "From Drawing to Story: Auto-Publish AI Video to YouTube with Blotato - PART 2 - vide",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# 🎬 From Drawing to Story — Auto-Publish AI Video to YouTube with Blotato\n\nTransform a hand-drawn sketch into a fully narrated, animated video — automatically generated and published to YouTube.\n\n> ⚠️ **This template is split into 3 separate workflows.**\n> Each part must be imported into its **own workflow** in n8n.\n\n---\n\n## 🎥 Tutorial\n\n@[youtube](bmx4IHX5lhI)\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ How It Works\n\n- **Part 1** — Analyze the drawing, generate character images & write the story\n- **Part 2** — Generate scene images with character consistency\n- **Part 3** — Generate videos, narrate with AI audio & auto-publish to YouTube\n\n---\n\n## 🔐 Credentials Needed\n\n- **[Blotato](https://blotato.com/?ref=firas)** — YouTube / TikTok publishing\n- **[AtlasCloud](https://www.atlascloud.ai?ref=8QKPJE)** — Kling Pro 3.0 video generation\n- **Anthropic** — Claude AI (story & prompts)\n- **ElevenLabs** — Narration audio\n- **Shotstack** — Final video assembly\n- **Nano Banana** — Image generation\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Setup Steps\n\n1. Configure credentials for each service above in n8n\n2. Set up a form trigger with a file upload field for the drawing\n3. Deploy the 3 workflows in order and connect them via webhooks\n4. Run a test submission with a simple sketch to validate the full pipeline",
        "height": 2000,
        "width": 816
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -2160,
        -368
      ],
      "id": "955a80f8-9e2f-4f13-a1fd-774d63cba56b",
